{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/976569-nam-in-wod","id":976569,"title":"Nam in WOD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T09:36:26-07:00","id":976569,"title":"Nam in WOD?","content":"has anyone run a campaing set during the Nam war? how was the experience","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:55:29-07:00","id":976642,"title":"","content":"Not for <b>World Of Darkness</b>, but I have played in a <b>Call Of Cthulhu</b> game based around the Delta Green covert ops setting. It took a lot from <b>Apocalypse Now</b> and the paranormal horrors were secondary to the human ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:31:20-07:00","id":976763,"title":"","content":"I cannot imagine anything more terrifying than mortal soldiers facing the native Fera and Kuei-jin of Vietnam. It might even explain why the USA had 58,000 KIA in Vietnam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:56:04-07:00","id":976776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/976569-nam-in-wod?p=976763#post976763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot imagine anything more terrifying than mortal soldiers facing the native Fera and Kuei-jin of Vietnam. It might even explain why the USA had 58,000 KIA in Vietnam.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD being what it is would probably bump those numbers up a bit. Also, the use of Agent Orange is an entire nightmare unto itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T18:21:10-07:00","id":976856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/976569-nam-in-wod?p=976763#post976763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might even explain why the USA had 58,000 KIA in Vietnam.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But with half a million NVA and Vietcong dead, perhaps Napalm had a terrifying effect on the Kuei-Jin as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T23:47:06-07:00","id":977017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/976569-nam-in-wod?p=976856#post976856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. But with half a million NVA and Vietcong dead, perhaps Napalm had a terrifying effect on the Kuei-Jin as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might also explain why a lot more of our deaths came AT night than during the day..<br /> <br /> Though on the fera angle, which group do you see as havnig more of a presence in the nam area..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:26:32-07:00","id":977037,"title":"","content":"It may be too controversial, because somebody can talk about William Calley and My Lai massacre, but another about the brutal massacre at Hue by the Vietcong. <br /> <br /> Do you know it? After that there a second war in 1978, Vietnam againts Cambodia, both comunist regimes, and that was the way how the Pol Pot's genocide ended, but China didn't like that and there was a brief conflict between Vietnam and China. Now in this age Vietnam doesn't trust China because this want to conquer near regions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:01:31-07:00","id":977322,"title":"","content":"Yes, which means that the US is allied with Vietnam. We could have saved a lot of time and effort if we had allied with Ho when he asked us to help him free Vietnam from the French in the '50s.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I see the Mokole being the most frightening Fera in Southeast Asia. Their animal forms were capable of good stealth at night and would have allowed them to kill enemy troops with minimal effort. That being said, if more than a handful of Mokole were active against the US, US casualties would have been catastrophic (a clutch Mokole could easily kill a company of soldiers within a single night). <br /> <br /> An interesting alternate reality setting could explore the consequences of having one hundred Mokole attacking US forces in Vietnam. With the combination of the traumatic effect of Delirium on humans, the ineffectiveness of infantry weapons against Mokole, and the regeneration of Mokole between attacks, you could have had a thousand US troops dying every week due to Mokole attacks. Can you imagine the effect of having 400,000 US troops MIA in Vietnam on the American psyche?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:36:18-07:00","id":977404,"title":"","content":"I always wanted to do a Werewolf game set in Vietnam inspired by Metal Gear Solid 3 and Apocalypse Now. A legendary pack of garou were sent into the jungle to investigate rumors of a risen bane, some visage o the Wyrm perhaps. They never returned, and the reports that have been coming in are... worrying. It seems the squad has gone native. Now the characters, under the auspice of US military command (coordinated by a US general who also happens to be a Silver Fang) are dropped into Vietnam, forced to square off against the native (and hostile) fera and kuei-jin, and eventually put down these legendary heroes who have carved out a caern in the heart of the country.<br /> <br /> I may have notes laying around somewhere. I'll see if I can dig them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T15:42:55-07:00","id":977437,"title":"","content":"Why would the Garou go to Vietnam when there were plenty of Wyrm Creatures in the USA in the 60s and 70s? The only reason they went into the Amazon in the 90s was Pentex environmental destruction. Heck, given the horrific environmental actions of the US military in Vietnam (Agent Orange anyone?), the Garou would be more likely to fight against the US military than for it (the Get would probably have gotten a boner from the idea of facing the most powerful army on Earth at that time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T18:29:52-07:00","id":977513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/976569-nam-in-wod?p=977322#post977322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, which means that the US is allied with Vietnam. We could have saved a lot of time and effort if we had allied with Ho when he asked us to help him free Vietnam from the French in the '50s.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I see the Mokole being the most frightening Fera in Southeast Asia. Their animal forms were capable of good stealth at night and would have allowed them to kill enemy troops with minimal effort. That being said, if more than a handful of Mokole were active against the US, US casualties would have been catastrophic (a clutch Mokole could easily kill a company of soldiers within a single night).<br /> <br /> An interesting alternate reality setting could explore the consequences of having one hundred Mokole attacking US forces in Vietnam. With the combination of the traumatic effect of Delirium on humans, the ineffectiveness of infantry weapons against Mokole, and the regeneration of Mokole between attacks, you could have had a thousand US troops dying every week due to Mokole attacks. Can you imagine the effect of having 400,000 US troops MIA in Vietnam on the American psyche?</div> </div> </div> </div>A full hundred? The Middle Dragons likely did not number anywhere near that much in the region. They're even scarier to compensate for their lesser numbers, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:58:59-07:00","id":977552,"title":"","content":"I do not know, I think that the Mokole probably have a population of 3,000 globally, which would make their population 1,500 in Asia. Whether or not they could have been convinced to attack the US military would be an extrapolation for an alternate history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T02:31:28-07:00","id":977670,"title":"","content":"Pentex could to have being sending tainted products to American army, and maybe also to Vietcong's Charlies. Vietcong may have be controlled or manipulated by kue-jins. <br /> <br /> Oriental feras, the hengeyokais, wouldn't allow war in their jungles but maybe only to cross them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:57:03-07:00","id":977765,"title":"","content":"I could imagine a scenario where Vietnam was lost because few US supernaturals wanted to help kill off rebellious farmers (there is no glory or honor is slaughtering inferior opponents).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:08:55-07:00","id":977851,"title":"","content":"Vietnam was won in the battlefield, but lost by the propaganda. It was showed like a Pyrrhic victory, and too unpopular for american people. Why to sacrifice oneself? <br /> <br /> Have you readen anything about the &quot;boat-people&quot; after the war?<br /> <br /> I imagine the WoD Vietcong like witch-hunters againts the supernatural creatures (feras, faes, Askashic brotherhood).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:45:31-07:00","id":977866,"title":"","content":"Vietnam was not won on the battlefield. If it had been, then the South Vietnamese would have been able to gain victory against the North Vietnamese. Unlike the North Koreans, the North Vietnamese did not have a million Chinese soldiers swarming across the border to save their bacon when the US was about to annihilate them.<br /> <br /> The Vietnamese did a damn good job beating the crap out of us while we were there, finished off the South Vietnamese when we left town, and then kicked the snot out of the Maoists when the Chinese tried to invade Vietnam. And, over forty years after they beat the crap out of us, they are now one of our valued trading partners and military allies against the growing Chinese imperialism in Asia. Once again, we would have been better off helping Ho when he first came around to ask for help. We should have accepted the Geneva Accords, just like the French did in 1954, and just made nice with the Vietnamese against the bigger threat of the Chinese and the Russians in the 1950s instead of wasting American lives and treasure (and a heck of a lot more Southeast Asian lives) just because of some misguided attempt to stop the independence of Southeast Asia from Western colonialism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:35:15-07:00","id":977897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/976569-nam-in-wod?p=977851#post977851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vietnam was won in the battlefield, but lost by the propaganda. It was showed like a Pyrrhic victory, and too unpopular for american people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you are referring to the fact that the Vietnam War was a decisive victory for the VietCong but some Americans believe we did not simply get our asses handed to us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T06:42:23-07:00","id":995607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/976569-nam-in-wod?p=977897#post977897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you are referring to the fact that the Vietnam War was a decisive victory for the VietCong but some Americans believe we did not simply get our asses handed to us.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vietcong was destroyed in the Tet Offensive and never recovered. South Vietnam lost the war because it was a failed state it's own people did not have the will to defend. Once the Americans left, the North Vietnamese army invaded and southern resistance collapsed. Victory for the North was inevitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:46:20-07:00","id":995653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/976569-nam-in-wod?p=995607#post995607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Vietcong was destroyed in the Tet Offensive and never recovered. South Vietnam lost the war because it was a failed state it's own people did not have the will to defend. Once the Americans left, the North Vietnamese army invaded and southern resistance collapsed. Victory for the North was inevitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Victory for the North was inevitable, I'll give you that.<br /> <br /> Seriously, you necro'd this thread for what, exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}